    "title": "Memphis Tigers volleyball announces eight-match spring schedule for 2026 - Memphis Standard",
    "text": "The University of Memphis volleyball team has released its 2026 spring schedule, which includes eight matches against teams from the Southeastern Conference and local programs.\nThe Tigers will begin their spring season on February 28 in Clarksville, Tennessee. The opening match is set for noon against Austin Peay, followed by games against Lipscomb and Cumberland (Tenn.) at the same venue.\nOn March 28, Memphis will return to Elma Roane Fieldhouse to play Alabama A&M at noon. Later that day, they will also compete against Rhodes College.\nThe team will travel to Tuscaloosa, Alabama, on April 11 for two matches against Power Four opponents. Memphis is scheduled to face Alabama at 2 p.m., followed by a match with Mississippi State.\nThe spring schedule concludes on April 17 with the Blue/White Scrimmage in Memphis. This event is scheduled for 6 p.m., and further details about the specific location will be announced later.\nFor more information about Memphis Tigers Volleyball and updates throughout the season, fans are encouraged to visit the team’s official website and follow their social media channels.",
    "summary": "The opening match is set for noon against Austin Peay, followed by games against Lipscomb and Cumberland (Tenn.) at the same venue. On March 28, Memphis will return to Elma Roane Fieldhouse to play Alabama A&M at noon. The team will travel to Tuscaloosa, Alabama, on April 11 for two matches against Power Four opponents. Memphis is scheduled to face Alabama at 2 p.m., followed by a match with Mississippi State. For more information about Memphis Tigers Volleyball and updates throughout the season, fans are encouraged to visit the team’s official website and follow their social media channels.",
